// KNOWN-PARTIALLY-BROKEN reference repro — NOT part of any test suite
// (does not reliably build — see below). Do not add to spec_tests/
// conformance, nova_tests, or any glob-discovered test path — kept here
// purely as an executable-by-hand diagnostic artifact for
// [M-consume-param-spawn-defer-active].
//
// Diagnosed 2026-08-01 (window p-ice-pack, п.11, sonnet). STATUS: PARTIAL
// FIX LANDED (see the commit touching compiler-codegen/src/types/mod.rs's
// `Stmt::ConsumeScope`/`ExprKind::Spawn` arms) — a real, independently-
// valuable CHECKER bug was found and fixed along the way: `spawn consume c
// { body }` (D415 §4 "already-bound" form, `c` already owned in the outer
// scope — a `consume` param or `consume x = expr` local) falsely reported
// [D133-not-consumed] on the OUTER `c` at ITS OWN enclosing scope-exit,
// even though ownership genuinely, synchronously transferred into the
// spawned child at the `spawn` statement itself. Root cause was TWO
// layers: (1) `Stmt::ConsumeScope`'s `re_consume=false` arm never marked
// the reused outer binding Consumed at all; (2) `ExprKind::Spawn`'s own
// `consume_walk_isolated_expr` wrapper snapshots/restores `ctx.states`
// around the whole body walk (sound for mut-captures, WRONG for an
// ownership move, which is synchronous at the spawn statement) — so even
// fixing (1) got silently undone by (2)'s restore. Both fixed.
//
// The ORIGINALLY-REPORTED codegen bug (`use of undeclared identifier
// '_defer_N_0_active'`) was NOT reached in a clean, isolated form this
// window — the D133 fix above unblocks TYPE-CHECKING the pattern, but
// actually BUILDING it hits, in order:
//   1. Without a declared `consume @cleanup(outcome ScopeOutcome)` method
//      on the moved type: `undefined symbol: Nova_<Type>_consume_cleanup`
//      — codegen unconditionally emits a cleanup call for this desugar
//      regardless of whether the checker validated one exists (itself a
//      separate, real gap — likely the same PLAN 217 "cleanup disarm"
//      machinery the original `_defer_N_0_active` report pointed at, but
//      NOT confirmed as the SAME bug).
//   2. WITH a declared `@cleanup`: a THIRD, differently-shaped bug —
//      `use of undeclared identifier '_nv_tmp_N'` inside the emitted
//      cleanup's ResourceTrace/error-path handling (a temp declared in one
//      C block, referenced from a sibling block that does not dominate it
//      — same STRUCTURAL class as [M-detach-box-while-loop-read-after]
//      п.2's box-scope-leak, but a DIFFERENT specific site).
//
// Reaching the EXACT originally-reported symbol name needs a repro shaped
// closer to the real TcpListener consume-param (which has its own,
// presumably more complete, `@cleanup`/close machinery) — out of this
// window's remaining budget after the checker-half fix + this triage.
//
// To reproduce the (now-fixed) checker false-positive:
//   nova check docs/plans/repro/m_consume_param_spawn_defer_active.nv
//   → BEFORE this window's fix: [D133-not-consumed] on `h`
//   → AFTER: clean ("ok")
// To reproduce the remaining codegen gap(s):
//   nova build docs/plans/repro/m_consume_param_spawn_defer_active.nv
//   → undefined symbol: Nova_MIceCpsHandle_consume_cleanup (no @cleanup declared here)
module nova_repro.consume_param_spawn_defer_active

type MIceCpsHandle consume { id int }
fn MIceCpsHandle consume @close() { }

fn use_handle(consume h MIceCpsHandle) Detach {
    supervised {
        spawn consume h {
            println("${h.id}")
            h.close()
        }
    }
}

fn main() Detach {
    use_handle(MIceCpsHandle { id: 42 })
}
